  <!-- ---------- the metaphor ----------
       A flask of water, standing in for a pair of lungs. Four properties the
       streak was missing, then the flasks drawn. -->
  <section class="cst-sec" data-chrome="light" aria-labelledby="met-h">
    <div class="cst-shell cst-shell--text">
      <h2 class="cst-h2 cst-mark cst-mark--coral" id="met-h">a vessel of water,<br>standing in for lungs</h2>
      <p class="cst-lead" style="margin-top:.85em">The health variable needed a form. A percentage on its own is a number you learn to ignore, and a lung diagram is a medical image people flinch away from. I used a flask of clear water: it starts pure, it clouds when you smoke, and it clears as you go without.</p>
      <p class="cst-p">It works as a mechanic rather than as decoration because water has the right physics built into the reader's head already. Nobody needs to be told that muddy water can be cleared, or that one drop of ink is not the same as a bottle. The metaphor carries the two properties the streak was missing — <strong>proportionality</strong> and <strong>reversibility</strong> — without a word of explanation.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cst-shell" style="margin-top:clamp(30px,5vh,60px)">
      <div class="cst-three">
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">proportional, so the cost is honest</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">One cigarette moves the value two points. It is a real loss and the interface does not soften it, but it is not framed as the destruction of everything you had built.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">reversible, so there is a way back</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">Clean intervals restore purity. This is the property a streak counter structurally cannot have, and it is the entire reason for choosing a fluid.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">continuous, so every day registers</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">Cutting from twenty a day to six is a large clinical improvement a streak scores as zero. The purity value moves, so the app can acknowledge reduction, not only abstinence.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

