  <!-- ---------- the rest of the system ----------
       Three supports around the central loop, each attached to the same record. -->
  <section class="cst-sec" data-chrome="light" aria-labelledby="sys-h">
    <div class="cst-shell cst-shell--text">
      <h2 class="cst-h2" id="sys-h">three supports around<br>the central loop</h2>
      <p class="cst-lead" style="margin-top:.85em">The purity variable answers what happens when you slip. It doesn't, on its own, give anyone a reason to open the app on an ordinary Tuesday. Three further pieces carry that load, and each one is deliberately attached to the same underlying record.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="cst-shell" style="margin-top:clamp(30px,5vh,60px)">
      <div class="cst-three">
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">streaks and challenges</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">A fourteen-day challenge with a progress ring, framed as a target you work toward rather than a possession you can lose. Weekly stats and history keep the trend visible even when a single day went badly, and a daily diary holds the context a number can't.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">the support network</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">Other people going through the same attempt, with forums, chat and groups. Connecting to other challengers carries a benefit, so the social feature has a reason to exist beyond being present — quitting <em>as</em> a group rather than being watched by one.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="cst-h3">resources you unlock</h3>
          <p class="cst-p">Health information and coping techniques, released by completing streaks rather than dumped in a library on day one. Gating means the material arrives when it's relevant — the one place I kept an unambiguous game mechanic, because the reward is genuinely useful.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cst-shell" style="margin-top:clamp(40px,7vh,84px)">
      <div style="background:var(--cst-surface,#F4F4F4);border-radius:clamp(12px,1.4vw,20px);overflow:hidden;padding:clamp(16px,3vw,40px)">
